+
+# autoescape-extension-case
+
+## Why
+`Flask.select_jinja_autoescape` only recognizes lowercase supported extensions,
+so templates such as `invoice.HTML` unexpectedly render without autoescaping.
+
+## What
+- Normalize the filename for the existing supported-extension check.
+- Add selector coverage for supported mixed-case names and retained behavior
+  for `None` and unsupported filenames.
+
+## Impact
+`Flask.select_jinja_autoescape` is supplied as Jinja's default `autoescape`
+callable by `Flask.create_jinja_environment`. This changes only its result for
+case variants of already-supported extensions; custom autoescape callables and
+all unsupported suffixes are unchanged.
+
+## Acceptance
+- [x] Supported extensions match regardless of filename case. — test:
+  `test_select_jinja_autoescape`
+- [x] `None` and filenames without supported extensions retain their prior
+  results. — test: `test_select_jinja_autoescape`
+- [x] The public test suite passes. — check:
+  `PYTHONPATH=src:.bench-pydeps python3 -m pytest tests -q`
